Patch 17: promote DC-block prediction level 2 to speed 2.

Standalone. Supersedes patch 0013 (which promoted it to speed 3) -- apply
INSTEAD of 0013, not on top; speed features cascade, so setting it at speed 2
covers speeds 2, 3 and 4.

This feature has been measured at three operating points and has never come
close to its bar:

    level 2 @ speed 4   +3.08% / +0.04%   ratio  77.0   (bar 20)
    level 1 @ speed 3   +3.08% / +0.00%   ratio ~308    (bar 25)
    level 2 @ speed 3   +5.22% / +0.04%  (A1)           ratio 130.5  (bar 25)
                        +1.99% / -0.00%  (A2)

Patch 0013 returned +5.22% on 4K at a BD-rate of four hundredths of a percent.
A feature clearing its bar by five times has that much unclaimed headroom, and
this specific move -- taking an existing assignment one preset slower -- is now
the most reliable mechanism found on this project. Six of the seven promotions
tried across both patch sets passed:

    tx_stats        s4->s3   ratio  34.0 (bar 25)   PASS
    dc_blk_pred L1  s4->s3   ratio 308   (bar 25)   PASS
    dc_blk_pred L2  s4->s3   ratio 130.5 (bar 25)   PASS
    warp_diamond    s4->s3   ratio  18.5 (bar 25)   borderline
    tx_stats        s3->s2   ratio  34.3 (bar 30)   PASS on A2
    ccso_early_term s2->s1   ratio  62.1 (bar 35)   PASS
    wienerns_iters  s2->s1   ratio 111.2 (bar 35)   PASS

Speed 2's bar is 30. Even if the ratio degrades as sharply on this promotion as
transform-statistics pruning did on its own (49.0 -> 34.0, a factor of 0.69),
130.5 would land near 90. This is the largest margin of any promotion still
available.

The honest caveat is that promotion has been measured to *reduce* the ratio
every time, because BD-rate grows faster than time saved. The question is never
whether the ratio falls, only whether it falls past the bar, and each promotion
starts from a lower ratio and faces a higher bar. This one starts far enough
above that the arithmetic is comfortable; the next one, to speed 1 against a bar
of 35, would not be.

-DAVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL=0 disables the promotion and restores patch-0013
behaviour without a patch edit.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
index f363519..ba14363 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
@@ -418,6 +418,33 @@ static void set_good_speed_features_framesize_independent(
   }
 
   if (speed >= 2) {
+    // Promote the DC-block predictor one preset further, to speed 2.
+    //
+    // This feature has now been measured at three presets and has never come
+    // close to its bar:
+    //
+    //   level 2 @ speed 4   +3.08% / +0.04%   ratio  77.0  (bar 20)
+    //   level 1 @ speed 3   +3.08% / +0.00%   ratio ~308   (bar 25)
+    //   level 2 @ speed 3   +5.22% / +0.04% A1, +1.99% / -0.00% A2
+    //                                        ratio 130.5   (bar 25)
+    //
+    // The speed-3 promotion returned +5.22% on 4K at four decimal places of
+    // BD-rate. A feature clearing its bar by 5x has that much unclaimed
+    // headroom, and every promotion in this family so far has paid: six of the
+    // seven tried across both patch sets passed.
+    //
+    // Speed 2's bar is 30. Even if the ratio degrades as sharply as
+    // transform-statistics pruning did on its promotion (49.0 -> 34.0, a factor
+    // of 0.69), 130.5 would land near 90.
+    //
+    // -DAVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL=0 disables the promotion without a patch edit.
+#ifndef AVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL
+#define AVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL 2
+#endif
+#if AVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL
+    sf->winner_mode_sf.dc_blk_pred_level = AVM_S2_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL;
+#endif
+
     sf->lpf_sf.early_terminate_ccso_search_by_cost = 1;
     sf->part_sf.partition_pruning_with_mlp_none_thresh = 2.5f;
     sf->part_sf.intra_cnn_split = 0;
